# KEYFRAME — Docker build-context filter. THE BUILD CONTEXT IS THE REPO ROOT.
#
# WHY THE CONTEXT MOVED UP, AND WHY THIS FILE HAD TO EXIST BEFORE IT COULD:
#
# render.yaml used to set `dockerContext: ./server`, and server/Dockerfile's only
# payload copy was `COPY . .` — so the image contained server/ and nothing else. The
# 135 frame packs live in <repo>/frames, one level ABOVE that context, which is outside
# the build entirely: no COPY, no bind, no symlink can reach up out of a context. The
# result in production was silent and total:
#
#   config.paths.root  = the server dir            (src/config.js: resolve(__dirname,".."))
#   resolveFramesDir() probes  <root>/../frames    -> /frames        (absent)
#                              <root>/frames       -> /app/frames    (absent)
#   -> returns null, logs "[frames] no frames directory found"
#   -> listPacks() returns []  ->  GET /api/frames serves an empty gallery,
#      the composer runs unstyled, and rotatedDefaultPack() has nothing to rotate.
#
# Dev never saw it because dev runs from the repo checkout, where ../frames resolves.
#
# Moving the context to the repo root fixes the reach — but it also drops 2.7 GB /
# 39k files into the build (1.2 GB .git, 585 MB server/node_modules, 249 MB
# asset_cache, 168 MB framecheck, 148 MB .cache, 105 MB web/, 60 MB of vendored
# reference trees). So the context is filtered down to what the RUNTIME reads: about
# 48 MB, dominated by the 33 MB of pack poster/preview media in server/public/frames.
#
# DENY-ALL, THEN ALLOW. `*` matches every top-level entry, dotfiles included, so this
# list fails CLOSED: the next big directory someone adds to the repo root is excluded
# until a human deliberately allows it here. The opposite shape — enumerate what to
# exclude — is what let the old server/.dockerignore quietly ship whatever appeared
# next to it.
#
# NOTE: `#` only starts a comment at the START of a line. A trailing comment after a
# pattern becomes part of the pattern, so every note below sits on its own line.
*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── the allowlist ──

# The app.
!server

# THE FIX. The published frame packs — 135 directories, 272 files, ~1 MB of FRAME.md
# + pack.json + media/audio contracts. This is the entire reason the context moved.
!frames

# The hyperframes/GSAP skill docs that services/skills.js injects into composer
# prompts. It probes <root>/../.agents/skills first and falls back to fetching them
# from GitHub at request time — so shipping these 0.8 MB makes production use the same
# text the templates were authored against, and removes a network dependency from the
# hot path of the first render after a cold start.
!.agents

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── carved back out of server/ ──
# (`!server` above re-includes the whole subtree; these later rules win over it.)

# Installed in the image by `npm ci` in the Dockerfile. Copying the host's tree would
# be 585 MB of the wrong platform's binaries (Windows/macOS builds of sharp, bcrypt,
# canvas) layered under a linux/amd64 runtime.
server/node_modules
**/node_modules

# Render/job runtime state. Render's disk is ephemeral and these are per-machine
# artifacts; baking a developer's job history into the image is 60+ MB of noise that
# the janitor would then try to reconcile against an empty db.
server/jobs
server/jobs.json
server/jobs.json.bak-*
server/public/videos
server/uploads
server/.last_job
server/.lastprisma
server/$OUT

# The admin template lifecycle store (src/templates/store.js: <root>/data/templates.json).
# Per-machine state, not source: baking a developer's records in would give production a
# catalogue of DRAFT templates whose pack directories are deliberately absent from the
# image. store.js mkdir -p's the directory and tolerates a missing file, so an empty
# start is the correct one.
server/data
server/.server*.log
**/*.log

# Machine-local caches: downloaded stock media (249 MB), the harvested-website cache
# (11.5 MB) and the hyperframes/Chromium scratch cache (148 MB). All are rebuilt on
# demand, and a poisoned harvest cache has already caused one production-shaped bug.
server/asset_cache
server/harvest_cache
server/.cache
server/asset_library

# Dev-only render harnesses and their output: framecheck contact sheets (168 MB),
# scrub frames, the showcase binaries (54 MB) and admin template working artifacts.
# Nothing under src/ reads any of them at runtime — only scripts/ does, and scripts
# that render are never run inside the container.
server/framecheck
server/scrub
server/showcase
server/_review
server/template_work

# SECRETS. These are gitignored so they are absent on Render, but a local
# `docker build` runs against the working tree where they very much exist, and a
# secret baked into an image layer survives every later `rm`.
server/.env
**/.env
server/config.json
server/auth-store.json

# The built web app. Vercel serves the frontend in this deploy (see
# DEPLOY-VERCEL-RENDER.md); the old server/.dockerignore excluded it too, so the
# container keeps serving public/index.html for a direct hit on the API host.
server/public/dist

# Elastic Beanstalk leftovers from an earlier host. Inert here, and confusing to find
# inside a Render image.
server/.ebextensions
server/.ebignore
server/.platform

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── explicitly not shipped ──

# UNPUBLISHED ADMIN TEMPLATES MUST NOT REACH PRODUCTION. `*` already excludes this,
# but that is an accident of ordering and this is a security property, so it is stated
# outright: publishing is a directory MOVE from frames_draft/ into frames/ (see
# src/templates/paths.js), and the whole point of the split is that a draft is never
# listed. A draft that shipped in the image would still not be listed — but it would
# be resolvable by name through packDir(), renderable, and readable as static pack
# media, which is exactly the exposure the two-root design exists to prevent. It is
# also untracked in git, so this line only matters for a local docker build; that is
# precisely the case where a half-finished template is sitting on disk.
frames_draft

# Not runtime inputs, and large: .git (1.2 GB), the Vercel frontend source (105 MB),
# the vendored reference trees, and the design/handoff libraries the composers cite in
# comments but never read. All are already covered by `*`; listed here so a future
# `!` line is written knowing what it would let in.
.git
web
old-templete
templete-design
screenshot
deploy
heygen-keyframes-video
pixabay-no-node-modules
blockframe-frame-pack
biennale-yellow-frame-pack
